# Anti AI Slop UI/UX

## Before coding UI

1. Define user goal, primary action, and required data — do not generate layout first
2. Read similar existing pages/components and match their pattern
3. Reference patterns: `app/pages/users.vue`, `app/pages/customers.vue`, `app/components/ConfirmModal.vue`

## Reuse (required)

- Nuxt UI: `UButton`, `UTable`, `UModal`, `UForm`, `UFormField`, `UInput`, `USelect`, `UBadge`, `UPagination`
- Shared components: `ConfirmModal`, `AppLoading`, existing `*FormModal.vue`
- Theme tokens from `app/app.config.ts` (primary: indigo, neutral: slate)
- Do not add UI libraries or one-off styled components without approval

## Forbidden slop patterns

- Decorative gradients, glassmorphism, heavy shadows, hero sections in admin pages
- KPI/chart cards without a clear business decision
- Multiple competing primary buttons on one screen
- Card nesting without information purpose
- Vague copy: "Welcome", "Manage efficiently", buttons labeled "Submit" / "Action" / "Click here"
- Icon-only critical actions without accessible label
- Arbitrary spacing (13px, 17px, 23px) — use 4/8/12/16/24/32 scale

## Required UX states

Every screen must handle: loading, empty, error, success feedback.
Destructive actions must use `ConfirmModal` with clear consequence text.

## Forms & data

- `UFormField name` must match Zod schema key
- `USelect`: use `placeholder`, never `value: ''` in items
- `$fetch` body: `{ ...state }` not reactive proxy
- Numeric IDs: use `??` not `||`

## Page structure (CRUD list pages)

```
Page header (title + primary action)
Toolbar (search, filters)
Table (priority columns only)
Pagination
Modal/Drawer for create-edit
```

## Pre-merge checklist

- [ ] User knows what to do without explanation
- [ ] One clear primary action
- [ ] Consistent with existing pages
- [ ] Mobile/tablet usable
- [ ] No decorative elements that do not support workflow
